finding: readFogInScatter does not honor stage 4's zero-where-readFog-is-identity contract at/before the camera near plane. In src/extras/fog/pipeline.ts, readFog clamps its slice fraction to zero for surfaceZ <= view.projection.x and samples the explicitly stored near-boundary (0,0,0,1). The new read instead passes that depth through fogCellCoordinate, obtains z=0, and clamp-to-edge samples feedback cell 0's lit RGB. With positive density, nonzero ambient or volumetric lighting, and an ordinary maxDistance, e.g. a camera near=0.1 and point=(0,0,-0.05), the integrated read is identity but the local read is nonzero. At exactly the near plane it additionally normalizes a zero vector. Add the near-boundary identity guard before constructing the ray and cover it with a lit-cell test; the new identity tests only exercise disabled/absent fog, so all pass despite this failure.
